# "Destroy up to one target nonland permanent. Its controller creates a tapped Powerstone token." The second sentence does
# not depend on the first: the attack trigger targets Bot2's Nutrient Block (indestructible, CR 702.12b), which survives
# (CR 701.8), and Bot2 still creates the tapped Powerstone.
# On turn 4 that Powerstone's {C} cannot pay the generic {1} of a nonartifact spell (CR 106.6): with Mox Jet's {B} and the
# Powerstone's {C} in the pool, Demonic Tutor ({1}{B}) is refused (Bot2 has no land and no other source). Cast with no target on turn 1 as in the other scenarios.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Cityscape Leveler
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Nutrient Block
Mox Jet
Demonic Tutor
Island x4
Island x10

